From: pixel2 ubuntu port
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: default to identity for MSM8998 MDSS

The Pixel 2 (walleye) bootloader leaves the display engine fetching when
it jumps to the kernel. Once mmss_smmu probes (~0.5 s) the enabled MDSS
node is put into a translated DMA domain with an empty page table, and
the next MDP fetch resets the SoC (no log; UFS isn't even up yet).
Removing "iommus" from the MDSS node avoids the reset, which pins it on
the SMMU attach. Newer SoCs' MDSS are already in this list for the same
continuous-splash reason; the msm driver attaches its own domain later.
---
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -411,6 +411,7 @@
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,glymur-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mdp4" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mdss" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8998-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8998-mss-pil" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,qcm2290-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sar2130p-mdss" },
